      },
      "content": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported",
      "level": 2,
      "section_number": "5.4",
      "section_id": "sec_5_4",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_6",
          "title": "6. Turn monitor off."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_5_4",
          "title": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_6",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 44,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0571",
      "reading_order": 621,
      "section": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 147.75,
        "t": 303.75375,
        "r": 539.1879499999995,
        "b": 236.99625000000003
      },
      "content": "The  replacement  level  supported  for  this  product  is  to  the  printed  circuit  board  (PCB assembly) and major subassembly level. Once you isolate a suspected PCB assembly, follow the procedures in Disassembly Guide section , to replace the PCB assembly with a known good PCB assembly. Check to see if the trouble symptom disappears and that the monitor passes all performance tests.",
      "section_id": "sec_5_4",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_6",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_6",
          "title": "6. Turn monitor off."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_5_4",
          "title": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported"
        }
      ],
      "page": 44,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0572",
      "reading_order": 622,
      "section": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 147.75,
        "t": 236.25374999999997,
        "r": 538.0619,
        "b": 182.99625000000003
      },
      "content": "If  the  trouble   symptom  persists,  swap  back  the replacement PCB assembly with the suspected malfunctioning PCB assembly (the original PCB assembly that was installed when  you  started  troubleshooting)  and  continue  troubleshooting  as  directed  in  this section.",
      "section_id": "sec_5_4",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_6",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_6",
          "title": "6. Turn monitor off."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_5_4",
          "title": "5.4 Replacement Level Supported"
        }
      ],
